            <ArticleTitle>Total pancreatectomy and islet cell autotransplantation: Definitive treatment for chronic pancreatitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>435-42</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3949/ccjm.83a.15056</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In appropriately selected patients, total pancreatectomy and islet cell autotransplant controls pain and improves quality of life while often minimizing the development of overt diabetes. Multidisciplinary management and lifelong follow-up help to maximize the benefit of this procedure. This review highlights its history, indications, metabolic outcomes, and future directions.</AbstractText>
